2026-09-04 20:09:36 | INFO | THE SYMMETRIC FILTER AND THE VARIANCE TARGET. The baseline runs h_t = omega + alpha_sym eps_(t-1)^2 + beta h_(t-1) with alpha_sym = alpha + gamma_lev/2, and the DGP's own unconditional variance solves sigma2_unc = omega / (1 - alpha_sym - beta) because E[eps^2 1{eps<0}] = E[eps^2]/2 under a symmetric law. E[h_t] therefore obeys the SAME recursion as E[sigma2_t] and matches the unconditional variance EXACTLY: the filter is unbiased in the mean and misspecified in the dynamics, which is what isolates leverage leakage from a level error. The witness sets omega = 0.04 * (1 - alpha_sym - beta) at every grid point (l.252-253), so sigma2_unc = 0.04 on all fifteen and the grid is variance-targeted.
